  "hypothesis": "H86I-KSAD: Blind Quaternary geothermal conduits and unmapped range-tip/accommodation-zone faults are distinguished from non-tectonic scarps and shallow volcanic noise by coupling (1) Roest 3-D magnetic analytic signal + 150 m harmonic upward-continuation depth-persistence + vector-consistent Laplace vertical gravity curvature g_zz = -(d_col B18 + d_row B11), (2) Morris-Byerlee-Kostrov azimuthal normal-dilation (cos^2(theta - 22 deg)) and Riedel shear (sin^2(2*(theta - 22 deg))) tendency projected onto the multi-physics spin-2 strike director, (3) 1-m LiDAR unilateral facing polarity |downface - upface|, sentinel-clean 10-m fluvial k_sn/chi steps, potassic K/Th alteration residual, and absolute-elevation zmean_m (1,180-1,345 m ASL) Lake Lahontan contour-parallelism deconfounding, and (4) SAR exposure-propensity PU + Elkan (2001) Bayes prior-odds calibration decoded via Minoux-exact Dinkelbach Submodular K3-Supremum Expected-DTI Allocation.",
  "mechanism": "Strict outer Leave-One-Quadrant-Out (quad != q eroded 1.2 km) + nested cross-component PU ensemble (26 quadrant-invariant physical planes + 6 fold-visible anisotropic Kostrov-Pollard crack-tip/stepover/shadow planes), calibrated via Elkan (2001) Bayes subsampling odds correction and decoded by maximizing the provably monotone-submodular Dinkelbach expected-DTI functional (1 - 0.2*0.17)*sum_y p(y)*max(0, K_3(x,y) - C_S(y)) - 0.2*0.17*(1 - M_hat(x)) at min_sep=2.4 px, collar d_cat > 2.6 px, budget_cap=37,654.",
  "named_non_fault_process": "(1) Pleistocene Lake Lahontan wave-cut shorelines (1,180-1,345 m ASL), suppressed by absolute-elevation zmean_m contour-parallelism; (2) symmetric V-shaped fluvial gullies, suppressed by unilateral 1-m LiDAR |downface - upface| polarity; (3) shallow basalt float and E-W (090 deg) GeoDAWN flight-line leveling seams, suppressed by 150 m upward-continuation attenuation and low normal dilation tendency T_d(90 deg) = 0.14.",
